AAREADME.TXT for the ISEE 3 (ICE) Hourly Ephemeris from the Data Pool Tape.

H. Kent Hills
April 28, 2000
--------------

This data set was generated at NSSDC by selecting data parameters from the
ISEE 3 data pool tape (binary) and converting to ASCII. The time resolution is
about an hour and 4 minutes. Data records that contained fill data for the
spacecraft position were not included in this data set. Only data items that
are not instrument-specific are included here. The data items, in order, are:
year, day of year (Jan. 1 = 001), seconds of day, bit rate code, maneuver
code, spin period average (in seconds) over the hour, and the GSE X,Y,Z
components of the spacecraft position (in km). The bit rate code is 1,2, or 4
for bit rates of 512, 1024, or 4028 bps, respectively. The maneuver code is 0
if there were no maneuvers during that time period (which can be up to an hour
and four minutes starting at the given time), and is 7 if there were any
maneuvers during that time. Record length is 78 bytes. The time period covered
is from soon after launch through the end of the primary mission, i.e., August
13, 1978 through February 7, 1987. 

In any publication using these data, please acknowledge the ISEE 3 / ICE
project and the National Space Science Data Center. 
